# Actions & selectors — placement and shape

## Context

`app/src/actions.ts` holds action creators (`addTask`, `toggleTask`,
`removeTask`, `setPriority`, `setFilter`); `app/src/selectors.ts` holds pure read
helpers (`visibleTasks`, `remainingCount`). Consumers use these instead of
building action objects or reading `state.tasks` by hand.

## Rule

- Every dispatchable action gets a creator in `app/src/actions.ts` that returns
  a typed `Action`; never build `{ type, payload }` objects inline at call sites.
- Action creators contain NO logic beyond assembling the payload — no state
  reads, no side effects.
- Derived reads go in `app/src/selectors.ts` as PURE functions of `AppState`
  (no mutation, no I/O); reuse a selector instead of filtering `state.tasks`
  again at the call site.
- Keep both files as named exports consistent with the `Action` union in
  `types.ts`.

## How to verify

1. `grep -rEn "type:[[:space:]]*\"" app/src --include=*.ts` finds action `type`
   literals only in `actions.ts`, `reducer.ts`, and `types.ts` — not in
   UI/consumer code.
2. Selectors take `AppState` (or a slice) and return data without mutating it.
3. Each action creator has a matching reducer `case` and union member.



